message.content:
I found two possible periapical lesions, and I'm not confident about either. I only looked at the image by eye, using zoomed and contrast-enhanced crops; no detection model or measurements were involved. Neither spot shows a clear, well-defined radiolucency, so I graded both as PAI 3.

1. **Lower right first molar** (left side of the image): there is a faint area of bone loss around the tip of the front root.
2. **Lower left first molar** (right side of the image): there is an ill-defined lucent area near the root tips, between the roots and toward the back. This could be bone loss between the roots rather than a true periapical lesion.

I also checked the upper premolars and molars on both sides. Some crowns have caries, but I couldn't see a clear lesion at any root tip there. A dentist should confirm all of this before it is used for anything clinical.

